   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Shader Swirl Tide\n\nSilky blue bands twisting into a deep navy whirlpool. A WebGL shader backdrop; the tide preset of shader-swirl.\n\nCategory: shaders. Length: 5.0 s. WebGL: yes.\n\nUse when:\n- A calm, silky whirlpool that feels deep rather than loud.\n- Foreground is light text or a bright product shot that needs a dark field around it.\n- You want a finished Swirl look without tuning the palette and parameters yourself.\n\nAvoid when:\n- The video must use your brand colors: start from `shader-swirl` and set `colors`.\n- You want a lighter, contrasting mood from the same shader: use `shader-swirl-citrus`.\n\nVariables:\n- colors (string): Colors, default \"#a9d6e5, #61a5c2, #2c7da0\"\n- color_back (color): Background, default \"#012a4a\"\n- speed (number, 0-8): Speed, default 1\n- band_count (number, 1-12): Bands, default 5\n- twist (number, 0-1): Twist, default 0.2\n- softness (number, 0-1): Softness, default 1\n- center (number, 0-1): Center, default 0.2\n- proportion (number, 0-1): Proportion, default 0.5\n- noise (number, 0-1): Noise, default 0.3\n- noise_frequency (number, 0-1): Noise frequency, default 0.4\n- rotation (number, 0-360): Rotation, default 0\n- scale (number, 0.1-4): Scale, default 1\n- offset_x (number, -2-2): Offset X, default 0\n- offset_y (number, -2-2): Offset Y, default 0\n- resolution (number, 0.25-1): Resolution, default 0.75\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
